Validation round 08 fixes (DCS Control, 2026-11-25): frame-generation settings live without a rebuild, and no
generation for swapchains no projection layer uses.
- apply_embedded_control no longer arms swapchains still flagged generation_eligible_pending. Each control revision
  armed DCS's early swapchains (enumerated, never named by a projection layer): four synthesizers that never composed a
  frame, the first live change stalling the frame thread 1.62 s and each later one about 0.63 s. A swapchain a
  projection layer uses is armed by the frame path, as at the start. Tested: live-ini with an unused swapchain (fake
  runtime, D3D12 / D3D11 / flight) makes no private swapchain and logs no ready record or history for it.
- [ofxr] dcs_motion_occlusion_fill set live per synthesizer (D3D12FrameSynthesizer::set_occlusion_fill), like the
  quality keys (set_fg_quality): the fill's pass is made with dcs_motion whatever the mode and the mode is read per
  pair (mode 1's Sharp HUD gate stays per pair). A fill-only change is no longer a rebuild in apply_embedded_control or
  at an arming thread's take-in, and a settings-only change keeps the arming thread's work. Tested: 0 -> 2 -> 1 -> 0 on
  a synthesizer made with the mode before gives the image of one made with the new mode, byte for byte.
- Flight log: cockpit_mask result=12 c bits 16-31 carry the fill's pixels (units of 65536); live_settings result=5,
  one record per synthesizer each time its settings are set (made, set live, rebuilt): quality keys, fill mode, why,
  whether its pairs can carry the fill, the composition's quality bits; b= the swapchain.
- OFXR_LiveFgContract ("DCSC-OFXR-LIVE-FG/2"), exported, so DCS Control can tell this live contract from 0104/0122's by
  the DLL's bytes.
- Keys off costs what 0.7.0 cost (validation round 08: comp+pack per pair in the 30-fps regime 214 -> 385 us with every
  new key off). The quality options' and the fill's code, never taken with the keys off, made every NVIDIA composition
  about twice the instructions (3X masked-MV composition 5244 -> 9403) and 3X's composition about 30 % slower on
  hardware (fg_triple_bench, 5424 x 5356 x 2, RTX: 2073 -> 2721 us; 2X 1240 -> 1345 us). frame_synthesis.hlsl now
  compiles them only with XRFG_FG_EXTRAS=1: every existing composition is the same bytecode as 0103's (checked with
  fxc), and an _extras twin of each of the 40 NVIDIA compositions (plain, masked, depth, MV, depth+MV) carries them.
  The synthesizer registers a twin for each composition it makes, binds it only for a pair with a quality bit or the
  fill's bit (pair_extras), and makes its pipeline on first use (at creation when the options already have a key on).
  Measured after the fix, keys off: 3X 2075 us, 2X 1229 us (0103: 2074 / 1229-1238). Keys on, 3X (2X): all quality
  keys 2746 (1349) us, fill 2 3206 (1499) us, both 3241 (1501) us. The DLL grows by about 4.8 MB.
- tests/fg_triple_bench.inc (XRFG_TEST_FG_TRIPLE_BENCH, label bench): the composition with DCS's mask and MVs in 2X and
  3X, keys from XRFG_TEST_FG_TRIPLE_QUALITY / _FILL; written so it builds against 0001-0103 too.

